Phase 3: Troubleshooting Steps to Record (Even if simulated!)

Issue 1 (Anticipated Subnet/IP Error): Realizing that a custom VPC doesn't automatically assign public IPs, and resolving it by adding associate_public_ip_address = true to your aws_instance blocks.

Issue 2 (Permission/Key Path Error): Verifying that your private key file has the correct local file permissions (e.g., running chmod 400 vockey.pem if Ansible throws a "permissions are too open" warning).

Issue 3 (SSH Timeout / Security Group): Confirming that port 22 inbound was explicitly permitted in your security group resource so Ansible wouldn't timeout trying to connect.
